Short:        Media player for every datatype
Uploader:     (We fill this in at upload time)
Author:       Dalsin Limited
Type:         mus/play
Version:      0.1.1
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.0
Distribution: Aminet

OpenPlay plays anything a datatype opens: pictures as a slideshow, sounds,
tunes and modules, and films, from one window with a playlist. A new
datatype is a new format for OpenPlay, with nothing else to install.

It is drawn with OpenGadTools in your OpenLook theme, light or dark, with
its buttons as icons (the default), icons and text, or text. Files and
drawers dropped on the window join the playlist; playlists save and open as
.opl and .m3u.
"About this file" says which datatype opened it and what decoded it.

With the Open datatypes and a services card or a paired Cradle (the
Nursery), it plays AVIF, HEIC, JPEG XL, WebP, FLAC, Ogg, MP3 and more. On an
AGA Amiga, Save CDXL turns a film into a CDXL the chipset plays by itself.

Requires AmigaOS 3.2 and a 68020 or better.

